{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"182","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Common Divisors"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Vasya has recently learned at school what a number's divisor is and decided to determine a string's divisor. Here is what he came up with."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"String "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the divisor of string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":" if and only if there exists a positive integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" such that if we write out string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" consecutively "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" times, we get string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":". For example, string \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"abab"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" has two divisors — \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ab"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"abab"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now Vasya wants to write a program that calculates the number of common divisors of two strings. Please help him."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first input line contains a non-empty string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s1"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second input line contains a non-empty string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s2"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Lengths of strings "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s2"},{"kind":"text","text":" are positive and do not exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"105"},{"kind":"text","text":". The strings only consist of lowercase Latin letters."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the number of common divisors of strings "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s2"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"abcdabcd\nabcdabcdabcdabcd\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"aaa\naa\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In first sample the common divisors are strings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"abcd"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"abcdabcd"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample the common divisor is a single string \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". String \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aa"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" isn't included in the answer as it isn't a divisor of string \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aaa"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"182D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/182/problem/D"}